From: idiazraz <100824525+idiazraz@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: omci: log MIB resets from the OLT

An OLT sends a MIB reset when it (re)provisions the ONU: after each
registration, and when it decides to start the configuration over. Log
it, so the line monitor can tell the user when the ISP re-provisioned
the box.
---
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -4233,6 +4233,7 @@
 		*content_len = 32;
 		break;
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_MIB_RESET:
+		dev_info(odev->parent, "OMCI MIB reset from the OLT\n");
 		if (omci_agent_mib_reset_locked(odev, false, profile_changed))
 			content[0] = OMCI_RESULT_PROCESSING_ERROR;
 		else
